{{else}}
## The runtime

The game is built on the {{engine.name}} engine, which documents itself in the
`engine/` directory at the root of this repository. It provides the gameplay
framework the game is written inside — worlds built from levels, game modes,
actors and their components, and the controllers that drive pawns — and it owns
the frame loop and the delta time the game is given, rendering, collision
detection, input actions, audio cues, asset loading, the canvas fit, and the
debug overlay. Read its documentation before you start. This specification
states only what is specific to Carom.
